A change to the thread whose turn another core has, as a bind to units of another core, does not tell that core,
whose timer stays deferred for a turn that should end at the next tick.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: the timer is set past a tick an unmarked change brought forward

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -347,7 +347,7 @@ static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
     if (sooner) {
         core->nearest_release = sched_ticks + fill;
     }
-    if (joined || sooner || is_turn(t)) {
+    if (joined || sooner) {
         core_notify(core);
     }
 }
